findFields:
You are given {N} photo(s) of the pages of one person's {DOC}. Find ONLY these fields:
{LIST}
Look at every photo, including small, faint or partly covered print. Return ONLY valid JSON — no prose, no markdown, no code fences — with one entry per field name above: {"fields":{"<field name>":{"value":"...","page":0,"box":{"x0":0,"y0":0,"x1":1,"y1":1}}}} where "page" is the 0-based number of the photo you read it on and "box" is a tight box around the value itself (not its printed label), as fractions 0 to 1 of that photo's width and height. For a field that is not printed on these photos or that you cannot read with confidence, use {"value":""}. Never guess.
